Below are some of the columns that will be useful for analysing CT‑series size and consistency, together with a short note on their possible usage.

• "SeriesInstanceUID": series identifier – used for grouping and filtering   
• "SeriesNumber"      : human‑readable series order – returned in final list  
• "PatientID"         : patient identifier – returned in final list  
• "instance_size"     : size (bytes) of every SOP instance – summed to obtain series size  
• "Modality"          : filter to CT only  
• "collection_id"     : filter out the “nlst” collection  
• "ImageType"         : exclude frames that contain the value LOCALIZER  
• "TransferSyntaxUID" : exclude JPEG‑compressed syntax UIDs  
• "Rows", "Columns"   : pixel dimensions – must be constant within the series  
• "PixelSpacing"      : spacing – must be constant within the series  
• "ImageOrientationPatient": orientation – must have exactly one value per series  
• "ImagePositionPatient"   : slice position – used to check z‑spacing, duplicates, etc.

The following exploratory Snowflake queries (all limited to 20 rows) move from simple inspection to progressively more complex checks.  
Remember: adjust filter predicates or hard‑coded literals as you learn more about the real data.  
All column names are wrapped in double quotes, and only the single table supplied (`IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL`) is referenced.

```sql
-- 1. Distinct collections available (quick sanity‑check on "nlst")
SELECT DISTINCT "collection_id"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct modality values to confirm CT spelling
SELECT DISTINCT "Modality"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Peek at a few CT rows that are NOT from NLST
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        "PatientID",
        "SeriesNumber",
        "ImageType",
        "TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND   "collection_id" <> 'nlst'
LIMIT   20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Which TransferSyntaxUID values appear in CT data (to spot JPEG UIDs etc.)
SELECT DISTINCT "TransferSyntaxUID"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "Modality" = 'CT'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count of CT instances that are *not* JPEG compressed
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "ct_uncompressed"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND  "TransferSyntaxUID" NOT IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70',  -- JPEG Lossless
                                   '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51'); -- JPEG Baseline
```

```sql
-- 6. Inspect ImageType values in CT (to see how “LOCALIZER” is encoded)
SELECT DISTINCT "ImageType"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "Modality" = 'CT'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Quick estimate of largest CT series by byte‑size (still ignoring many constraints)
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        "PatientID",
        "SeriesNumber",
        SUM("instance_size") / 1048576.0 AS "series_size_MiB"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   "Modality" = 'CT'
  AND   "collection_id" <> 'nlst'
  AND   "TransferSyntaxUID" NOT IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70',
                                    '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51')
  AND   ( "ImageType" IS NULL OR "ImageType" NOT ILIKE '%LOCALIZER%' )
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID", "PatientID", "SeriesNumber"
ORDER BY "series_size_MiB" DESC
LIMIT   20;
```

```sql
-- 8. For a chosen SeriesInstanceUID, confirm there is only one ImageOrientationPatient
-- (replace the sample UID with a real value from query 7 results)
SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
        COUNT(DISTINCT "ImageOrientationPatient") AS "n_unique_orientations"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   "SeriesInstanceUID" = '<<REPLACE_WITH_SERIES_UID>>'
GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT   20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Check slice spacing & duplicates for a chosen series
-- Extract z‑coordinate from ImagePositionPatient[3] and look at deltas
SELECT  "InstanceNumber",
        "ImagePositionPatient",
        TRY_TO_DOUBLE( SPLIT_PART("ImagePositionPatient"::STRING, ',', 3) )  AS "z_mm"
FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE   "SeriesInstanceUID" = '<<REPLACE_WITH_SERIES_UID>>'
ORDER BY "z_mm"
LIMIT   20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Draft of the full filtering logic to surface candidate series
-- (still capped at top‑5 by size; refine if intermediate checks show edge‑cases)
WITH filtered AS (
    SELECT  "SeriesInstanceUID",
            "PatientID",
            "SeriesNumber",
            SUM("instance_size") / 1048576.0             AS "series_size_MiB",
            COUNT(*)                                      AS "n_images",
            COUNT(DISTINCT "ImageOrientationPatient")     AS "n_orient",
            COUNT(DISTINCT ("Rows" || 'x' || "Columns"))  AS "n_dim",
            COUNT(DISTINCT "PixelSpacing")                AS "n_pixsp",
            COUNT(DISTINCT "ImageType")                   AS "n_imtype",
            COUNT(DISTINCT "ExposureTime")                AS "n_exptime"
    FROM    IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
    WHERE   "Modality" = 'CT'
      AND   "collection_id" <> 'nlst'
      AND   "TransferSyntaxUID" NOT IN ('1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70',
                                        '1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.51')
      AND   ( "ImageType" IS NULL OR "ImageType" NOT ILIKE '%LOCALIZER%' )
    GROUP BY "SeriesInstanceUID", "PatientID", "SeriesNumber"
)
SELECT *
FROM   filtered
WHERE  "n_orient" = 1         -- single orientation
  AND  "n_dim"    = 1         -- identical Rows x Columns
  AND  "n_pixsp"  = 1         -- identical PixelSpacing
  AND  "n_imtype" = 1         -- consistent ImageType
  AND  "n_exptime"= 1         -- consistent exposure
ORDER BY "series_size_MiB" DESC
LIMIT  5;
```

The final query sketch (#10) already applies most of the requested conditions; you can extend it by

• computing the z‑axis direction‑cosine cross‑product check,  
• verifying slice‑interval regularity and duplicate‑slice absence, and  
• ensuring that the number of unique z positions equals `n_images`.

Replace the placeholder `<<REPLACE_WITH_SERIES_UID>>` in queries 8 & 9 by a real SeriesInstanceUID obtained from earlier queries when you drill further into a candidate series.
